# Copy this file to config.env and edit for your setup. The real config.env is
# gitignored (it names your accounts); this example is committed.

# Swap when the ACTIVE account's 5h utilization is at or above this (0-100).
FIVE_HOUR_PCT=80

# Swap when (max weekly - min weekly) across accounts is at or above this (0-100).
# This is the base dead zone; it tightens adaptively as the lowest account's weekly
# usage (the floor) climbs toward 100, so the rotator keeps rebalancing near the ceiling.
WEEKLY_DIVERGENCE_PCT=10

# Adaptive dead zone: when the floor (min weekly) is at or above HI_FLOOR, the
# divergence threshold shrinks to HI_PCT; at or above VHI_FLOOR it shrinks to VHI_PCT.
WEEKLY_DIVERGENCE_HI_FLOOR=80
WEEKLY_DIVERGENCE_HI_PCT=5
WEEKLY_DIVERGENCE_VHI_FLOOR=90
WEEKLY_DIVERGENCE_VHI_PCT=2.5

# systemd timer cadence, in minutes.
INTERVAL_MIN=15

# Per-account weekly ceiling (0-100). An account at or above ITS OWN ceiling is capped:
# the rotator moves the pointer off it, never swaps onto it, and releases an operator PIN
# held on it. The PIN file is retained at this reserve threshold so it resumes once
# weekly resets, but is cleared automatically when known weekly usage reaches 100.
#
# The gap below 100 is a reserve for the surfaces this rotator does not control. The Claude
# mobile and desktop apps spend the SAME seven_day allowance the rotator polls, and they do
# it whether or not the CLI is pointed at that account. So an account you also use from your
# phone wants a ceiling below 100, or unattended background work will drain it to the limit
# and your phone stops working. An account used only for background work can sit near 100.
#
# Do not set a ceiling of exactly 100. Consumers treat the ceiling as an ADMISSION check and
# nothing meters mid-job, so work admitted at 99 runs past 100 and fails hard.
WEEKLY_CEIL_DEFAULT=98
# Per-account overrides, WEEKLY_CEIL_<label>. Unset accounts use the default above.
#WEEKLY_CEIL_acctA=95
#WEEKLY_CEIL_acctB=99

# Required: space-separated account labels, one per bootstrapped account.
ACCOUNTS="acctA acctB"

# Codex labels are configured independently from Claude labels. The same label
# may appear in both lists because each rotator has its own store and sentinel.
CODEX_ACCOUNTS="acctA acctB"

# A Codex swap only reaches running work once the app-server is replaced, because
# it caches its account at startup. Set to 0 to leave the app-server alone.
CODEX_APPSERVER_RESTART=1

# Backstop for the case where the app-server is replaced by signal and the external
# supervisor that was meant to respawn it (Codex Desktop, on its next connect) never
# does. A later live tick that finds nothing listening restarts this unit to bring an
# app-server back, instead of concluding there is nothing to restart and leaving the
# box unable to run any Codex work. Empty disables it, which is the default. Never
# name user@N.service here: it is the per-user session manager, and the rotator
# refuses it for that reason.
# CODEX_APPSERVER_BACKSTOP_UNIT="codex-remote-control.service"

# The app-server is found by whichever pid is listening on this socket.
# CODEX_APPSERVER_SOCKET="$HOME/.codex/app-server-control/app-server-control.sock"

# Restarting the app-server interrupts every running turn, so the rotator refuses to
# swap while this probe reports work. Non-empty stdout means in flight; a non-zero
# exit is treated as in flight. Unset uses the bundled codex-inflight-all.sh. Set to
# empty to disable the gate (tests, or a machine with no app-server).
# Override only if the probe lives somewhere else.
# codex-inflight-all.sh unions two signals: codex-inflight.sh asks the app-server which
# threads are running, covering every Codex client on the box (Desktop, the CLI, and any
# external dispatcher) at once, and drain-inflight.sh adds bonus-drain's own record of
# jobs it dispatched outside that daemon. Either arm reporting work holds the swap.
# Pointing this at codex-inflight.sh alone drops the dispatcher arm.
# CODEX_INFLIGHT_CMD="/path/to/ai-token-rotator/codex-inflight-all.sh"

# Claude side: same gate, same contract. Swapping the live credential under a running
# session redirects its next API call to another account, which bills the wrong weekly
# allowance and falsifies any dispatcher's accounting. Unset uses the bundled
# drain-inflight.sh with the claude provider; empty disables the gate.
# INFLIGHT_CMD="/path/to/ai-token-rotator/drain-inflight.sh claude"
